# The Sewer Pros — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. `.env.local` is gitignored.
#
# Only PUBLIC identifiers belong in this file. Never commit secrets,
# API keys, or private credentials (CLAUDE.md §52, §86). Anything
# prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ is inlined into client-side JavaScript and is
# readable by anyone who loads the site.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Canonical site origin  — REQUIRED for build
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bare origin. No path, no query, no fragment.
#
#   correct    https://example.com
#   accepted   https://example.com/      (normalised to no trailing slash)
#   rejected   example.com               (no scheme)
#   rejected   https://example.com/site  (has a path)
#
# The build FAILS if this is unset. That is intentional: this project
# uses `output: 'export'`, so the origin is baked into canonical tags,
# schema @id values, and the sitemap as static text with no runtime
# correction possible (docs/02 §53, docs/15 §5).
#
# ⚠ The production value is NOT YET DECIDED — PENDING-001 covers both
# the domain and the apex-vs-www choice. Do not guess it and do not
# commit a guess. For local development use a placeholder host you will
# recognise as non-production; never point this at a real domain you do
# not control, and never let a preview host reach production metadata
# (docs/02 §88, CLAUDE.md §53-54, §88).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Analytics  — not yet implemented (build sequence step 23)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GA4 measurement ID. Public by design.
#
# ⚠ Never send PII into analytics: no names, emails, phone numbers,
# street addresses, or form message bodies (docs/19 §-, CLAUDE.md §40).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=
